---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Dose Easy - Support"
  description="Need help with Dose Easy?"
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/dose-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>
        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Dose Easy?</p>
          <p>Contact <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Dose%20Easy%20Support" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> for help with reminders, checklist setup, and history review.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do reminders work?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Each dose time gets a reminder that names what’s due, with a button to mark it as taken. Times whose doses you’ve already taken stay quiet. Turn reminders on or off in Settings → Reminders. They’re scheduled on your iPhone; no account is needed.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I mark a dose as taken?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Tap the dose on Today, or on the Dose Easy widget. Touch and hold a dose on Today to skip it. To catch up on a day you forgot, open History, pick the day and tap the dose.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I see how my routine is going?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes. History shows the month at a glance, how many of your doses you took over the last 30 days, your streak of days with every dose taken, and each supplement on its own. You can export everything as a CSV file from History or Settings.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Dose Easy store cloud backups?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">No. Your routine and history stay on your iPhone, and are included in your device’s own backups.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Dose Easy tell me what to take?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">No. Dose Easy is a tracker, not medical advice. It doesn’t recommend supplements or amounts. Ask your doctor or pharmacist what’s right for you.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
